{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/927805-skills-but-no-resources","id":927805,"title":"Skills but no Resources","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-07T15:35:39-07:00","id":927805,"title":"Skills but no Resources","content":"I thought I'd come here since this has come up multiple times during play. How do you decide how much money certain skills can produce? If someone is very good with Crafts but didn't take any dots in resources how much does each success equal in money? Can it basically replace the skill? Does it take more time than usual? What about expression as someone who sings/plays and encourages tips? Many skills are marketable but I was curious what was the best way to decide how much, especially with crafts(painting).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T15:54:47-07:00","id":927811,"title":"","content":"An abstract amount of money that is enough money to take care of your basic needs and any recurring expenses you might have (bills, investments, loan payments, etc.) but not enough to leave you with any disposable income, since disposable income is what Resources represents. You might also be able to exchange your services for goods, or barter with the things you produce. That's largely covered under ST fiat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-07-2016, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T16:04:35-07:00","id":927817,"title":"","content":"For the second thing Charly said, you could use the Cash item to represent the goods or service done. Just target an Availability and use an extended action with success needed based on that Availability. Then when they sell it, it is worth that level of Cash (which is worth that much of item in Availability again when they want to spend it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T18:22:37-07:00","id":927883,"title":"","content":"There are rules for how both politics and larceny can be used as resources but I forget the specifics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T19:51:28-07:00","id":927915,"title":"","content":"Procuring equipment rules, &quot;Availability and procurement&quot;. <br /> My advice on the issue: don't be stingy with allowing people to pay for things with skills, as it develop their characters and usually takes at least one scene of time, and that's actually a pretty valuable resource. Make Resources Merit a thing for getting stuff on demand, skipping the &quot;time tax&quot;, and without having to justify why skill x allows you to procure equipment y.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T05:41:15-07:00","id":928072,"title":"","content":"Thanks that all works great. I was having issue and you guys made it much simpler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T10:35:25-07:00","id":928246,"title":"","content":"I usually have the players explain their characters' occupations at the beginning, then assume they have the normal equipment and salaries from it. Merits like Resources and Professional Training means you have something <i>more</i> than what one would expect, like a particularly high-skill position, or a solid investment paying dividends. Really, it doesn't come up enough for me to question what the characters are buying: a box of bullets, a pile of scrap, a meal at a cafe, gas in the car, a new hunting knife, a box of matches, a book on the monster that's kidnapping people to weave them into plants and drain their memories into a cup for a tasty drink... These aren't hard for the average person to pay for, and it's not worth stopping the players from acting to worry about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}